    "diff_hunk": "@@ -9610,6 +9610,32 @@ partial /*sealed*/ interface <dfn>Document</dfn> {\n \n   </div>\n \n+  <p>DOM nodes whose <span>node document</span> do not have a <span>browsing context</span> are\n+  exempt from all document conformance requirements other than the <a href=\"#writing\">HTML\n+  syntax</a> requirements and <a href=\"#writing-xhtml-documents\">XHTML syntax</a> requirements.</p>\n+\n+  <div class=\"example\">\n+\n+   <p>In particular, the <code>template</code> element's <span>template contents</span>'s <span>node\n+   document</span> does not have a <span>browsing context</span>. For example, the <span\n+   data-x=\"concept-element-content-model\">content model</span> requirements and attribute value\n+   microsyntax requirements to not apply to a <code>template</code> element's <span>template\n+   contents</span>. In this example an <code>img</code> element has attribute values that are\n+   placeholders that would be invalid outside a <code>template</code> element.</p>\n+\n+   <pre>&lt;template>\n+ &lt;article>\n+  &lt;img src=\"{{src}}\" alt=\"{{alt}}\">",
